  This assertion verifies that the builder() method correctly instantiates and returns a new Builder object. This is fundamental to the Builder pattern implementation, ensuring clients can begin the fluent construction of ApigeeLlm instances.

Scenario 2: Verify builder() returns distinct Builder instances on each call

Details:
  TestName: builderReturnsDistinctInstancesOnEachCall
  Description: Verify that each call to builder() returns a new, distinct Builder instance, ensuring no shared state between builders.
Execution:
  Arrange: No setup required.
  Act: Call ApigeeLlm.builder() twice to obtain two Builder instances.
  Assert: Assert that the two Builder instances are not the same object (using assertThat with isNotSameInstanceAs).
Validation:
  This assertion confirms that the builder() method creates a fresh Builder instance on each invocation. This is critical for thread safety and preventing unintended side effects when multiple ApigeeLlm instances are being constructed concurrently or sequentially.

